		{"id":"7f18ef75ea15b10b","x":-29,"y":-240,"width":300,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"# Map Generation"},
		{"id":"9df4f9f08d9d6312","x":-680,"y":47,"width":457,"height":505,"type":"text","text":"1. Storing a tile-map\n\nTile:\n\tA set of images grid governed by internal state\n\nTile Set:\n     A group of tiles of the same type.\n\nTile Map:\n     The group of all tile-sets used to create a map which the player can interact with.\n\nMap:\n     A struct that contains its own tile-map, along with the grid that defines the tiles in the tile-map, the hash of all of the tile positions."},
